WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:11.803
Endpoint Detection and Response is a security capability that monitors endpoint activity, detects suspicious behavior, supports investigation, and helps responders contain or remediate threats.

2
00:00:11.803 --> 00:00:16.034
The detection part helps teams notice unusual or risky activity.

3
00:00:16.034 --> 00:00:19.975
The response part helps teams act before an incident spreads further.

4
00:00:19.975 --> 00:00:35.241
EDR tools typically collect telemetry from endpoints, such as process execution, file activity, network connections, registry changes, login activity, script execution, and suspicious command-line behavior.

5
00:00:35.241 --> 00:00:40.639
This telemetry gives analysts a more detailed view than a simple allowed or blocked message.

6
00:00:40.639 --> 00:00:43.174
The goal is not only to block known malware.

7
00:00:43.174 --> 00:00:50.008
The goal is to help security teams understand what happened, how far it spread, and what action should be taken next.

8
00:00:50.008 --> 00:00:56.374
EDR is especially useful when an event is not obviously good or bad and the analyst needs context.
